plugin.wasm
writing-tools-plugin-v*.zip

# The third-party corpora the tools/ generators read. Downloaded rather than
# committed: WordNet, SCOWL and MyThes come to 46MB between them, they are
# read only when a dataset is regenerated, and the outputs they produce -- the
# .gz files beside this -- are what the plugin actually ships. See README.md
# for where each comes from. The two hand-written files in data/ are committed,
# since nothing can regenerate those.
data/wordnet/
data/scowl/
data/th_en_US_v2.dat

# The datasets are embedded compressed; only the .gz files are committed.
# Keeping the plain text alongside them would be the same data twice, free to
# drift. Regenerate with the tools/ commands, then run build.sh.
words-en-US.txt
words-en-GB.txt
common-en-US.txt
common-en-GB.txt
thesaurus.txt
definitions.txt
exceptions.txt
inflections.txt

.DS_Store
